From 5591f1f54124095159139f9c6d87fb855de535b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Franklin <cfranklin4474@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:37:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] mm: add tier_ext, per-lruvec reclaim policies in BPF

Add a BPF struct_ops type, tier_ext_ops, whose instances attach to the
lruvecs of one memcg on a set of NUMA nodes. Reclaim of those lruvecs
consults the policy at these points, and falls back to the classic LRU or
MGLRU behaviour whenever the policy has no opinion:

  lruvec_shrink  skip the lruvec in this reclaim pass
  swappiness     per-lruvec anon/file balance
  folio_scan     keep/evict a folio at the cold end of the lists
  folio_reclaim  keep/evict an isolated folio after its references were
                 counted, optionally forbidding or requiring demotion
  folio_added / folio_accessed / folio_evicted  notifications

KEEP and SKIP are ignored at reclaim priority 0 so a policy cannot make
memory unreclaimable. Per-policy counters live in
/sys/kernel/debug/tier_ext.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
